    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`add_business_days` is implemented in `solution.py` and the test suite in `tests/test_solution.py` passes (35 tests, `python -m pytest -q tests`). The function validates inputs first: `start` must be a `date` and not a `datetime`, `n` must be an `int` and not a `bool`, and every holiday must be a `date` and not a `datetime`. It collects holidays into a set, so generators work. For `n == 0` it moves forward until it reaches a weekday that is not a holiday. For `n != 0` it steps one day at a time in the right direction and counts only business days, so `start` is never counted. The tests cover forward, backward and zero cases, weekend and holiday handling, the input forms, and each `TypeError` path. I could not run a coverage tool because the shell is restricted to the test command. By reading the code, every executable line is reached by at least one test, so I expect coverage well above the 90% gate, but that is unmeasured.",
